---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import ArticleSchema from "../../components/ArticleSchema.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Pre-Litigation Disputes · Pro Se Fair Play Mediation"
  description="Mediation before anyone files. What a signed agreement means when no case exists, and how to file a family case with an agreement already in hand."
>
  <ArticleSchema slug="pre-litigation-disputes" />
  <!-- ========================== HEADER ========================== -->
  <header class="article-header">
    <div class="container article-header-inner">
      <Breadcrumbs trail={[{ href: "/process", label: "The Mediation Process" }]} current="Pre-Litigation Disputes" tone="light" />
      <p class="kicker reveal reveal-d1">
        <span class="kicker-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        Before You File
      </p>
      <h1 class="display article-title reveal reveal-d2">
        Pre-Litigation <span class="display-italic">Mediation</span><span class="display-italic">.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="lede reveal reveal-d3">
        Most people think of mediation as something that happens after a case is
        filed. It does not have to be. Sitting down before anyone files keeps the
        decision with the two of you, and keeps the courthouse in reserve.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <!-- ========================== BODY ========================== -->
  <section class="article-body">
    <div class="container-narrow article-prose">
      <h2>Mediating Before a Case Exists</h2>
      <p>
        Pre-litigation mediation is simply mediation that happens first. Both
        sides agree to sit down before a petition or complaint is filed. There is
        no case number, no filing fee, and no judge assigned. Nothing is on a
        court calendar, so nothing is on a court clock.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is voluntary on both sides. One party cannot require the other to
        attend, which is why the first step is usually a conversation about
        whether the other side is willing.
      </p>

      <h3>What a Signed Agreement Means</h3>
      <p>
        This is the part that works differently. When a case is already pending,
        the parties file a signed agreement with the court and it is folded into
        a final judgment. With nothing filed, there is no case to file it into. The
        signed agreement is a contract between the parties, binding on them the
        way other contracts are. If a case is filed later, that agreement can be
        presented to the court then.
      </p>

      <h3>If You Do Not Reach Agreement</h3>
      <p>
        Nothing is lost and nothing is waived. The court route stays exactly
        where it was, and either party can still file. In practice even an
        unfinished session tends to narrow what is actually in dispute, which
        makes anything that follows shorter.
      </p>

      <h2>Business and Civil Matters</h2>
      <p>
        Not every dispute is a family matter. These are handled as private
        mediation, chosen by both parties rather than ordered by a court.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Contract and service disagreements.</li>
        <li>Business partners and small-business owners.</li>
        <li>Unpaid invoices and payment disputes.</li>
        <li>Disagreements between family members over a shared obligation.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        If the dispute is about property specifically, see
        <a class="link-underline" href="/process/real-estate-mediation">Real Estate Mediation</a>.
        Rates for business and civil matters vary with the nature and complexity
        of the dispute, so please ask during booking.
      </p>

      <h2>Filing a Family Case With an Agreement in Hand</h2>
      <p>
        For divorce and parenting matters there is a second reason to mediate
        first. Couples who reach an agreement before filing can file an
        uncontested case rather than a contested one, arriving with the terms
        already settled and signed instead of asking a judge to decide them.
      </p>
      <p>
        The documents that agreement turns into are prepared separately, through
        <a class="link-underline" href="/services/parenting-plan">Parenting Plan Preparation</a>
        or the
        <a class="link-underline" href="/services/court-packet">Turn-Key Court Packet</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>How Mediation Helps</h2>
      <p>
        Filing is a decision, not an inevitability, and it is much easier to make
        once you know what the other side will actually agree to. Mediating first
        answers that question at the point where you still have every option
        open.
        <a class="link-underline" href="/process/how-mediation-works">How mediation works</a>
        walks through what a session looks like.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ========================== CLOSING CTA ========================== -->
  <section class="article-cta">
    <div class="container-narrow article-cta-inner">
      <a class="btn btn-primary article-cta-btn" href="/book">
        Book a Free, Private Consultation
        <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
      <p class="scheduling-note">Flexible Scheduling Available: Evening and Weekend Mediations to Accommodate Your Busy Life.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* ============================================================
     HEADER — cream, mirrors the legal pages
     ============================================================ */
  .article-header {
    position: relative;
    padding-block: clamp(4rem, 6vw + 1rem, 6rem) clamp(2rem, 3vw, 3rem);
    background:
      radial-gradient(ellipse at 80% 20%, rgba(196, 154, 75, 0.08), transparent 55%),
      var(--color-cream);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-divider);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .article-header-inner { position: relative; max-width: 64rem; }
  .article-title {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-size: var(--step-5);
    line-height: 1.04;
    color: var(--color-navy);
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    max-width: 20ch;
    font-weight: 400;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .article-title .display-italic { color: var(--color-gold-deep); font-weight: 400; }
  .article-header .lede {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    max-width: 62ch;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
  }

  /* ============================================================
     BODY PROSE
     ============================================================ */
  .article-body {
    padding-block: var(--space-lg) var(--space-3xl);
    background: var(--color-cream);
  }
  .article-prose {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
  }
  .article-prose p { max-width: 64ch; }
  .article-prose p + p,
  .article-prose ul + p { margin-top: 1.25rem; }
  .article-prose h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--color-gold);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--step-3);
    line-height: 1.1;
    color: var(--color-navy);
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    font-weight: 400;
  }
  .article-prose h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
    padding-top: 0;
    border-top: none;
  }
  .article-prose h3 {
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-variation-settings: "opsz" 24;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    line-height: 1.25;
    color: var(--color-navy);
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .article-prose ul {
    margin: 1rem 0 1.25rem;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    max-width: 64ch;
  }
  .article-prose li { line-height: 1.55; }
  .article-prose strong { color: var(--color-navy); font-weight: 600; }

  /* ============================================================
     CLOSING CTA — button only
     ============================================================ */
  .article-cta {
    position: relative;
    padding-block: var(--space-lg);
    background: var(--color-cream-warm);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-divider);
  }
  .article-cta::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0 0 auto 0;
    height: 1px;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, var(--color-gold) 40%, var(--color-gold) 60%, transparent);
    opacity: 0.7;
  }
  .article-cta-inner { display: flex; justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .article-cta-btn {
    background: var(--color-navy);
    color: var(--color-cream);
    border-color: var(--color-navy);
  }
  .article-cta-btn:hover {
    background: var(--color-navy-deep);
    color: var(--color-cream);
    border-color: var(--color-gold);
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .article-title { font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 1.8rem + 3vw, 3.5rem); }
  }
</style>
